**How to implement.** The online sources' offline snapshots get a location of their own, read like every other (001 §G 'Every path is overridable in appsettings.json; a Launcher Data locations panel shows them'; the S13.1 brief: the offline snapshot lives under a DataLocations sources folder; .spec-md §3.9 'No test touches the user's data'; .spec-md §8: no configuration knob other than the 001 §G locations). A snapshot is slow data that every kit shares, so its default sits beside the library database under `%LOCALAPPDATA%` (001 §G), never in Documents. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`: `DataLocations` (step 81) gains, last, `materialSourcesFolder : FolderName`, with a one-line doc: the folder holding each online source's offline snapshot. `defaultsUnder` answers it as `FolderName "%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Sources"`, written there alone. `DataLocationKind` (step 192) gains, last, `MaterialSourcesLocation`, documented in one line naming its field, and `all` lists it last, so the kinds still follow the record's fields. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs` (step 193): `caption` answers `Online source snapshots` and `uiKey` `MaterialSources` for it; and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs`' `DataLocations.rows` (step 193) answers the kind's row as it answers every other folder's, showing and opening `materialSourcesFolder`, so the Data locations window lists the folder with Open folder and nothing else in the view changes. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs` (step 82): module `ConfigKey` gains `materialSourcesFolder` = `"MaterialSourcesFolder"` with a one-line doc naming its field; `readDataLocations` reads it through `readSetting` exactly as it reads the other folders, its default written back when missing or refused; and `resolveLocations` expands it and roots it at `install` as it does the others. (4) The test run: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/appsettings.json` (step 82) gains `MaterialSourcesFolder` = `TestRun/Sources` in `appSettings`, and `TestAppScope.testLocations` (step 83) holds `Sources` under the owner's folder, which `fileLocations` (step 88) moves with the rest, so no test reaches `%LOCALAPPDATA%`. Every other construction of a `DataLocations` record sets the field: `DataLocationsTests` (step 193) sets a `Sources` folder under its test folder. (5) Tests, their assertions widened to the new location and nothing else changed: `WorkbenchSettingsTests`' `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text` also requires the sources default above, and `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field` requires the eight kinds, `MaterialSourcesLocation` last. `DataLocationsTests`' `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file` requires eight rows, the last showing and opening the sources folder. `AppConfigTests`' `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded` also requires the `MaterialSourcesFolder` default written back verbatim and answered expanded, and `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output` requires six folders under the test output, the sources folder among them.

**Acceptance.** After the location lands, `DataLocations` MUST hold `materialSourcesFolder`, defaulting beside the library database and read from `MaterialSourcesFolder` in `appsettings.json`, and the Data locations window MUST list it with Open folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the widened `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text`, `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field` and `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file`, the count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the widened `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded` and `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
